# phios contain — deny list, consulted only for `phi-contain --workdir`.
#
# One path or glob per line, '#' starts a comment, '~' expands to the real
# user's home. --workdir is refused when it resolves inside one of these
# roots. This is a guard-rail on the argument the caller typed, not the
# containment boundary — the boundary is the mount set a profile's own
# .paths file declares, and a root listed here is still reachable if a
# profile binds it in directly.

~/.ssh
~/.gnupg
~/.password-store
~/.local/share/keyrings
~/.mozilla
~/.librewolf
/etc
/root
/proc
/sys
/boot
